// The film table: every film Kuvert ships, once. Lists refer to films by id and add only what is theirs:
// the built-in list its shelves (catalogue.js), the Academy's ballots their fields (ceremonies.js), the
// envelopes their notes (curated.js). Swedish titles are in js/i18n/titles-sv.js and posters in posters.js,
// both keyed by the same ids. SEAGAL's filmography is its own joke and stays in catalogue.js.
//
//   t, y        title and year: together they made the permanent id, which never changes afterwards
//   tri, ord    the series a film belongs to, and which part it is
//   aka         the title as the Academy printed it on the ballot, where that differs
//   wd, tmdb    the film on Wikidata and on TMDB (the TMDB id is Wikidata's own statement, P4947)
//   rt, dir, g  runtime in minutes, director and genres: Wikidata statements (CC0), read on the day in `at`.
//               An envelope film has none here: its note in curated.js carries them, for the edition it recommends
//   ref         references the runtime statement carried
//   via         a named source used instead of Wikidata, for the fields it lists (runtime and director
//               unless it says otherwise), with the day it was read
//   moods       hand-picked moods; without them, moods are suggested from the genres (basics.js)
//   note        the edition note that goes with a named source: "cuts", "editions" (basics.js), or its own text
//
// The sourcing rules are in docs/EDITORIAL.md. To add a film: `node tools/film-facts.mjs "Title" 1999`
// prints its line. `npm run check:catalogue` checks every list against this table.
